<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4026.18">
  <DUT Name="ST_PackMLCommands" Id="{5e4501d0-0012-4d19-9a41-000000000001}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    The nine PackML unit commands, as one value a caller can fill in and hand
    over whole - an HMI writes it, a supervising unit writes it, a test writes
    it, and none of them needs nine separate arguments.

    Every field is a LEVEL, not a pulse: the state manager decides whether a
    command means anything in the state it is currently in, so a command that
    arrives too early is ignored rather than queued, and one that is held past
    the transition it caused does not cause it a second time. That is what
    makes a stuck HMI button harmless.
*)
TYPE ST_PackMLCommands :
STRUCT
	Reset : BOOL;
	Start : BOOL;
	Stop : BOOL;
	Hold : BOOL;
	Unhold : BOOL;
	Suspend : BOOL;
	Unsuspend : BOOL;
	Abort : BOOL;
	Clear : BOOL;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
